<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Portugal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Portugal was a monarchy on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, formed during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a> against the Almoravid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> states. From the fifteenth century it launched voyages that built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. It clashed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> over trade, engaged closely with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a>, and its court's move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> preceded the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Portugal" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tonyjeff, based on ancient national symbol. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Portugal_(1830%E2%80%931910).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
